screens.summary:
Gantt with one column per business day. Padding 28 48 24. There is a 280px label column, and the chart width W is measured with a ResizeObserver (1456px at 1920).

Top bar:
- Eyebrow 'Timeline'. Title 'Three months' / 'Two weeks'.
- Mono subtitle: '28 Sep 2026 – 15 Jan 2027 · 77 business days', or '5 Oct – 16 Oct · 10 business days' in 2w.
- Legend: BAU, Project, Past target, Previous plan, Milestone, Target, Overload.
- Pan controls: 32x32 chevrons plus 'This week'. Visible in 2w only.
- Zoom segmented control '2 weeks | 3 months'. A sliding ink pill 96px wide, positioned at left 3px or 99px.

Zoom windows:
- 3m: T0 Mon 28 Sep to T1 Fri 15 Jan. That is 77 BD columns plus 15 gap slivers of 5px each. Weekends and holidays collapse into one sliver per run.
- 2w: 10 BDs (Mon of the current week plus wk×7), with 18px slivers. wk is clamped to [-1, 13].

Chart rows:
- Date header, 80px, four tiers:
  - months: 13/600, label pinned when clamped, hidden if narrower than 70px;
  - ISO weeks 'W41' in mono 10;
  - day pills: '5' in 3m or 'Mon 5' in 2w; today is inverted ink;
  - BD numbers: '3' / 'BD3'; BD1 in ink.
- Capacity row, 76px, caption 'Hours per day against 8h. Notched = BAU, solid = project.':
  - one vertical stack per BD at 5px/hour, with a dashed 8h line at bottom 51px;
  - BAU notches use a repeating gradient of 4px fill and 1px gap;
  - projects use a soft fill with an accent outline;
  - overload turns red with a one-shot pulse;
  - tag 'FI move · Mon 4 Jan'.
- Lanes (scroll area). Group header 40px; BAU row 38px; rotation row 48px; project row 64px.
  - 'Private Credit · BAU': one tick per occurrence, 4px wide in 3m. In 2w it is wide with text 'Returns · 6h'. After the move or once handed over, it is drawn outlined.
  - 'Private Credit · Projects'.
  - 'Fixed Income · BAU': the 'Eurozone sovereign rotation 4h/day' row. Segments are Build (solid, soft fill) or Refresh (dashed). Codes show in 3m, 'Germany · Build' in 2w. Note: 'Starts Mon 4 Jan with Germany, first Build pass →'.
  - 'Fixed Income · Projects'.
- Project row, left side: name, a Roll of the forecast date, and a delta chip.
- Project row, right side, layered:
  - ghost of the previous plan (dashed, opacity 0.55);
  - forecast bar;
  - risk overrun from target to forecast;
  - milestone diamonds (filled once passed);
  - forecast end diamond;
  - target Γ marker;
  - flash ghost end diamond plus 'was 27 Nov';
  - 'moved +N BD' chip;
  - off-range label 'Target Late Mar 2027 →'.
  - Define status draws a hatched bar.
- Overlay lines: today (1px ink) and the FI move (1.5px fi-accent).
- Footnote: 'Weekends and UK bank holidays are collapsed to slivers. Hover a row to trace it through the capacity strip; click for details.'

Hover and tooltip:
- Hovering a row sets the global hover; everything else dims to 0.28.
- A 300px cursor tooltip is positioned imperatively. Variants: day, routine, rotation, project, milestone.

Clicking a project row opens a 460px side panel (no scrim). It contains:
- domain chip and close button;
- name, and the goal in serif 24px;
- facts: Forecast, Target, Against target, Confidence 'N of 5', Last check-in;
- milestone list;
- 'Open workspace' and 'Tell Remi' buttons.

Zoom and pan re-lay out every element with 440ms spring transitions.

engineAlgorithms.spec:
remi.v1 shape:
- projects[] in stored shape;
- tasks {id: bool}; doneOn {id: ISO};
- feed[] (its 'when' is a display string);
- funds bool[12] (today's r-ret run); routines[];
- bauDone {'rid:ISO': ISO};
- notes {ISO: [{id, t: 'HH:MM', text}]};
- m2: true.
Migration m2 inserts man-0 into manco now[0] if it is missing.

Mapping:
- Project fields map to the entity tables. Now blocks become now-horizon milestones with their tasks. Next items become next-horizon milestones. Explicit milestones are kept.
- 'ov' becomes HourOverride. scope from/to 'D Mon' strings must be resolved to ISO dates in the right year.
- checkins become CheckIn records.
- tasks and doneOn become task done flags and doneAt.
- bauDone becomes RoutineRun rows. funds becomes RunChecklistTick rows for r-ret on the import-day occurrence.
- Note t becomes createdAt = day + t in the local timezone.
- Feed 'when' values are unrecoverable; use the import time.

Textbook: sections, pages (tree via parent), blocks, and chart html strings → ChartAsset. The src marker 'charts/price-yield.html' maps to the bundled sample.

components.description:
Grid 26px | 1fr | auto.
- 16×16 checkbox button (aria-label 'Toggle'): border 1.5px, radius 3px, check glyph 13px with the same transitions as the 18px variant.
- Text: 13px; the item text with done styling + ' · <sub>' in muted. The sub is 'BD3' for BAU rows or the project short name for project rows.
- Due label in mono 11px:
  - done: 'done 5 Oct' (--ink-faint, 400);
  - overdue: 'overdue N BD' (color-mix(risk 45%, ink), 600);
  - due today: 'today' (--ink, 600);
  - otherwise 'Thu 15 Oct' (--ink-muted, 400).

Milestone rows prefix the text with '◆ '. Hover sets the global hover to the routine id or project id. Dims to 0.3.

Odometer-style rolling text; the prop is value (string). Used for fundsDone and mo.doneN.

Numeric values matching /^([+−-]?)(\d{1,3})(?:\.(\d))?(\D*)$/ are split into columns:
- a sign column (['', '+', '−']);
- 3 digit columns, left-padded with '' (empty cells collapse to zero width);
- a '.' column;
- a one-decimal digit column;
- a static suffix.

Date values like 'Wed 2 Dec' roll the weekday, digits and month.

Each column is a 1.25em-tall overflow:hidden window. Inside it is a vertical stack of all possible cells, translated by translateY(-index×1.25em) with transition: transform var(--dur-slow) var(--spring-soft), which is 440ms. A hidden copy of the full text sizes the element; the rolling layer is aria-hidden. Line-height 1.25, inline-block, baseline aligned.

dataConsumed:
model.F: formatter helpers keyed by day number. The ones Today uses:
- s(n) → 'Mon 5 Oct';
- dm(n) → '5 Oct';
- l(n) → 'Monday 5 October';
- mon(n) → 'Oct';
- monL(n) → 'October';
- d(n) → 5;
- iso(n) → '2026-10-05';
- dn(iso) → day number.

model.CAL: business-day calendar.
- days[n] = {n, iso, w (0=Sun), m (0-based month), d, y, bd (bool), bdm (BD index within the month, starting at 1, or null), hol (name or null)};
- bds: sorted array of business-day numbers;
- idx: map from day number to its index in bds;
- nextBD(n), addBD(n, k), bdDiff(a, b) = idx[nextBD(b)] − idx[nextBD(a)].

model.P: derived projects[]. Fields Today reads:
- id, name, short, goal;
- accent ('var(--pc-accent)' or 'var(--fi-accent)');
- domainName ('Private Credit' / 'Fixed Income');
- forecastN (number|null);
- now: [{m: milestoneName, due: iso, tasks: [{id, t: text, h: hours, due?: iso}]}];
- next: [{m, due}];
- milestones: derived and sorted [{name, date: iso}];
- forecastS, sinceLabel, checkin (these three feed only the unused prompt).

model.routines: derived routines[]. Fields:
- id, name, short, domain, kind ('monthly'|'weekly'|'daily'), bd, wd, h;
- stage (0 Manual, 1 Automating, 2 Shadowed, 3 Handed over), stageName;
- ruleShort ('BD8' | 'Weekly · Tue' | 'Daily');
- next: first 3 occurrences on or after TODAY, [{n, s, after, today}].

interactions:
Click a month-snapshot checkbox (only the 16px square is the button, not the whole row):
- the returns row for TODAY: m.setAllFunds(!allFundsDone), which ticks or unticks all 12 funds;
- any other BAU row: m.toggleBau('<routineId>:<iso>'), which stores the ISO of TODAY as the done date;
- a project task: m.toggleTask(id);
- a milestone row: m.toggleTask('ms:<pid>:<name>').

Hover (mouseenter) sets the global hover id, and mouseleave clears it with setHover(null). Hover sources:
- plan rows: the Returns card ('r-ret'), other BAU rows, focus blocks;
- capacity bar segments (except free);
- week mini-bar segments;
- week chips (a milestone chip uses its project id);
- week project items;
- month rows (routine id or project id).
Every element tied to a different id dims to opacity 0.3 (0.25 for bar segments), with a 140ms ease-out transition. Hover state lives in the shell, so it cross-highlights between the capacity bar, plan, week strip and month list.

Hover styles:
- week card background becomes ink 3.5% (via !important, so it also overrides the selected background);
- 'Routine' / 'Workspace' / 'Show more' buttons turn --ink (no transition);
- the 'Back to today' border turns --ink-faint.

motion:
Checkbox tick:
- background and border-color: 140ms ease-out;
- glyph opacity 0→1: 140ms ease-out;
- glyph scale 0.4→1: 180ms cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.5, 0.64, 1), an overshoot 'pop'. Under reduced motion the scale is always 1.
- Label colour: 240ms ease-out.
- Strike-through appears instantly.

algorithms:
dayLoad(n) (shell), computed for every BD.

BAU items:
- If n < MOVE: every routine with stage < 3 that occurs on n is added as {kind: 'bau', domain: 'pc' (hard-coded), h: r.h, name: r.short || r.name}.
- Otherwise: the rotation segment containing n gives {id: 'rot', kind: 'bau', domain: 'fi', h: 4, name: '<country> · <Build|Refresh>'}.

Project items: for each project with startN ≤ n ≤ (forecastN ?? targetN), take the first rule that applies:
1. h = p.ov[iso] if an override exists;
2. else if n ≥ MOVE, h = rateAfter;
3. else if bdm = 3, h = bd3;
4. else if bdm = 8, h = bd8;
5. else h = rate.
The item is added if h > 0.

Totals: bau = Σ BAU h, proj = Σ project h, total = bau + proj, free = max(0, 8 − total), over = total > 8.

backendImplications:
A Today/day-plan endpoint, e.g. GET /api/today?date=YYYY-MM-DD, returning:
- the header: date, bdm, monthBDs, kicker metadata, verdict;
- the load;
- the focus blocks: project, hours, the sliced tasks, the next milestone, and empty-state reason;
- other BAU rows;
- the next BAU run when the day has none.
The task-slicing algorithm (cumulative hours offset by earlier days' allocation from today) should run server-side or in a shared util, so Timeline/Calendar get the same answer.

risksAndQuirks:
Hard-coded copy and values in Today:
- '8h working day', 'of 8h planned', '…h of 8h' (it should use CAPACITY);
- the Returns card gutter '6h' (it should be the routine's h);
- 'BD3, monthly' (it should be the routine's ruleShort);
- 'of 12 funds' and fundsPct = done/12 (it should use FUNDS.length);
- 'BAU · Private Credit' on the Returns card;
- the '4h a day' fallback for the rotation.

localState:
Instance fields (not state):
- this.ft: day-switch timeout handle, cleared on unmount;
- this._req: the last dayReq.t handled.

backendImplications:
Schemas (schemas/): use a discriminated union for the change objects:
- task_done {project_id, task_id}
- task_add / scope_add {project_id, text ≤120, hours 0.25..80}
- blocker / note {project_id, text ≤160}
- confidence {project_id, value int 1..5}
- target_move {project_id, date ISO}
- hours_per_day {project_id, value (0,8]}
- bau_done {routine_id}
The envelope is {summary: str, changes: Change[], unplaced: str[≤4]}. Prefer structured output / tool-use JSON over the greedy regex.

risksAndQuirks:
applyCheckIn is called for EVERY project with any accepted change, even a target move alone. So it always:
- writes a check-in record ('Plan confirmed.' if there is no text), updates the checkin date and drops the stale feed item;
- sets blocker = d.blockers || null, silently CLEARING an existing blocker;
- keeps only the FIRST blocker when there are several.
When hours/day moved the forecast without scope, the feed says 'Forecast holds at <new date>', which is misleading.

components.description:
Exact block, identical in Foundations and Remi.dc.html:
--paper: oklch(0.975 0.007 85); --paper-raised: oklch(0.99 0.004 85); --ink: oklch(0.23 0.012 70); --ink-muted: oklch(0.47 0.012 70); --ink-faint: oklch(0.58 0.01 75); --hairline: oklch(0.9 0.008 80);
--pc-accent: oklch(0.5 0.1 128); --pc-accent-soft: color-mix(in oklch, var(--pc-accent) 13%, var(--paper)); --fi-accent: oklch(0.5 0.1 265); --fi-accent-soft: color-mix(in oklch, var(--fi-accent) 13%, var(--paper));
--risk: oklch(0.7 0.13 70); --overload: oklch(0.56 0.17 28); --done: oklch(0.74 0.008 85); --focus: oklch(0.35 0.02 80);
--font-ui: "Albert Sans", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; --font-display: "Libre Caslon Text", Georgia, serif; --font-numeric: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
--radius-s: 3px; --radius-m: 6px;
--space-1: 4px; --space-2: 8px; --space-3: 12px; --space-4: 16px; --space-5: 24px; --space-6: 32px; --space-7: 48px; --space-8: 64px;
--dur-fast: 140ms; --dur-base: 240ms; --dur-slow: 440ms;
--ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);
--spring-soft: linear(0, 0.049 5%, 0.156 10%, 0.283 15%, 0.408 20%, 0.522 25%, 0.62 30%, 0.702 35%, 0.769 40%, 0.864 50%, 0.922 60%, 0.956 70%, 0.976 80%, 0.987 90%, 1);
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){ :root{ --spring-soft: steps(1, jump-start); } }
The app also adds :root[data-motion="reduced"]{ --spring-soft: steps(1, jump-start); } for the in-app Motion tweak.
Global CSS: html,body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--font-ui);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased} (the app adds height:100% and text-rendering:optimizeLegibility). button,input,textarea{font:inherit;color:inherit}. a{color:var(--ink);text-decoration-color:var(--hairline);text-underline-offset:3px} a:hover{color:var(--pc-accent)}. The app adds ::selection{background:color-mix(in oklch, var(--pc-accent) 22%, transparent)}.
Colour roles as documented:
- --paper: page background
- --paper-raised: drawer preview, palette, inputs
- --ink: text, primary buttons, today
- --ink-muted: secondary text, 6.3:1 on paper
- --ink-faint: idle checkboxes and separators, not for body text
- --hairline: rules and outlines
- --pc-accent: Private Credit; --pc-accent-soft: PC project fills and chips
- --fi-accent: Fixed Income; --fi-accent-soft: FI project fills and rotation
- --risk: at risk (overrun past target, stale)
- --overload: a day over 8h
- --done: done, shown as a quiet strike-through
- --focus: focus border on inputs
Group notes:
- Paper and ink: 'Warm off-white paper, near-black ink. Saturation stays under 0.01.'
- Domains: 'One accent per domain; same lightness and chroma, different hue. Soft tints derive from the accent.'
- Status: 'Used sparingly. Chip text mixes the status colour into ink so it holds 4.5:1.'
